# Authors and Contributors

This file lists the people who have contributed to
terraform-provider-technitium. It is maintained by hand; if you have
contributed and are not listed, that is an oversight rather than a judgment,
and a pull request adding yourself is welcome.

Contributors retain copyright in the work they author. Individual source files
name their own copyright holder, and the project is licensed under MPL-2.0
throughout. See LICENSE.

## Maintainer

* Alex Ackerman (@darkhonor)

## Contributors

Listed in order of first contribution.

* batumilove (@batumilove) - forwarder (`FWD`) record support, made usable end
  to end in v1.2.1. Added `dnssec_validation` to `FWD` record identity and
  import IDs so two otherwise-identical forwarders can be told apart in
  Terraform state, with backward-compatible parsing of the legacy three-field
  form; fixed the import parser writing a CAA tag into the `protocol`
  attribute, a partial update silently disabling DNSSEC validation, and a
  permanent diff on records that omit the attribute. (#69)

* Aleman <aleman@ackermans.lt> - co-author on the forwarder record work above.
  (#69)

* Ujstor (@Ujstor) - cluster bootstrap and join (`technitium_cluster`,
  `technitium_cluster_secondary`, with `terraform import` support and
  adoption-safe replacement semantics), single sign-on (`technitium_sso`),
  local user and API token management (`technitium_user`,
  `technitium_api_token`), zone query-access and RFC 2136 dynamic-update ACLs
  (#89), web service TLS settings, and the record refresh fix for a missing
  parent zone (#88). Field-tested against a three-node cluster bootstrap and a
  roughly 200-resource adoption converging to a clean no-op plan. (#94)

* bytestrom (@bytestrom) - found and privately reported the API token leak in
  request URLs (GHSA-27mx-6hfq-f887), and fixed it: `Authorization: Bearer`
  token transport by default, the `legacy_token_auth` opt-out for pre-15.0
  servers, and query-string redaction of transport errors. (#121)

* Pushkar Anand (@pushkar-anand) - record `comments` support on `technitium_record`,
  so an in-place update no longer erases a comment set in the web console.
  (#139)

* Stefano Bertelli (@bartei) - DHCP server management: the
  `technitium_dhcp_scope` and `technitium_dhcp_reserved_lease` resources, the
  `technitium_dhcp_scope`, `technitium_dhcp_scopes`, and
  `technitium_dhcp_leases` data sources, plan-time validation, and the client
  layer behind them. Written in his fork, bartei/terraform-provider-technitium,
  and ported onto this tree from there.

* Dustin Sweigart (@dustins) - ported the DHCP work above onto this tree, and
  fixed two bugs in it: scope updates wiping standalone reserved leases (the
  `reservedLeases` parameter is now omitted when the attribute is unset), and
  every plan of a `for_each`/`count` scope failing on unknown values in
  ValidateConfig; regression tests for both.
